{"name":"Rain Shadow","hex":"#677276","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rain shadow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of diminished precipitation on the lee side of mountains, caused by the prior release of moisture on the windward side."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain_shadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rain shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A rain shadow is an area of significantly reduced rainfall behind a mountainous region, on the side facing away from prevailing winds, known as its leeward side."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Himalaya_composite.jpg/330px-Himalaya_composite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain_shadow","wikidata":"Q747173"},{"title":"Rain Shadow (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Rain Shadow is an Australian television drama series which premiered on 7 October 2007 on ABC TV. It aired on Sundays at 8.30 p.m. The six-part series was produced by Southern Star. Music from The Audreys features in the soundtrack for the show, including the main theme."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain_Shadow_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q7284485"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain","wikidata":"Q7925"},{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow","wikidata":"Q160020"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Rain_shadow_effect.jpg/500px-Rain_shadow_effect.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Rain_shadow_effect.jpg/500px-Rain_shadow_effect.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Effect of a rain shadow","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARain_shadow_effect.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Algeria.A2002118.1040.250m.jpg/500px-Algeria.A2002118.1040.250m.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Algeria.A2002118.1040.250m.jpg/1280px-Algeria.A2002118.1040.250m.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Algeria.A2002118.1040.250m.jpg/500px-Algeria.A2002118.1040.250m.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Atlas Mountains' (top) rain shadow effect makes the Sahara even drier.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlgeria.A2002118.1040.250m.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/A_virtually_cloudless_image_of_Madagascar_ESA230211.jpg/500px-A_virtually_cloudless_image_of_Madagascar_ESA230211.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/A_virtually_cloudless_image_of_Madagascar_ESA230211.jpg/1280px-A_virtually_cloudless_image_of_Madagascar_ESA230211.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/A_virtually_cloudless_image_of_Madagascar_ESA230211.jpg/500px-A_virtually_cloudless_image_of_Madagascar_ESA230211.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The mountain ranges on the eastern side of Madagascar provide a rain shadow for the country's western portion.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_virtually_cloudless_image_of_Madagascar_ESA230211.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ghat_satellite_view.jpg/500px-Ghat_satellite_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ghat_satellite_view.jpg/500px-Ghat_satellite_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The eastern regions of the Western Ghats lie in a rain shadow, receiving far less rainfall.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGhat_satellite_view.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Envisat_image_of_the_southern_Caspian_Sea_ESA223952.tiff/lossy-page1-500px-Envisat_image_of_the_southern_Caspian_Sea_ESA223952.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.or